<mei meiversion="5.0" xmlns="http://www.music-encoding.org/ns/mei">
  <meiHead>
    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title>Diffusa est</title>
      </titleStmt>
      <pubStmt/>
      <notesStmt>
        <annot>Old Roman gradual of the Lateran basilica, 12th century; f. 33v. Neume division, shapes and facsimile zones: a close reading of the Vatican Library's image of f. 33v (October 2026), written in the central-italian hand on the manuscript's red F line, with three lines (D, a, c) added to make a four-line staff.</annot>
      </notesStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
        <source>
          <bibl>
            <title>Diffusa est</title>
            <idno type="siglum">Vat. lat. 5319</idno>
            <idno type="shelfmark">Vatican City, Biblioteca Apostolica Vaticana, Vat. lat. 5319</idno>
            <ptr target="https://digi.vatlib.it/view/MSS_Vat.lat.5319"/>
            <idno type="cantus-id">g01397</idno>
            <note type="genre">Gradual</note>
            <note type="mode">5</note>
            <note label="manuscript" type="description">Old Roman gradual of the Lateran basilica, Rome, 12th century: the Roman chant dialect, not the Gregorian melody. Central Italian neumes (nota romana) on a red F line with letter clefs. The gradual Diffusa est, f. 33v.</note>
            <note label="manuscript" type="title">Graduale (Old Roman)</note>
            <note label="manuscript" type="transcription">Read note by note from the Vatican Library's photograph of f. 33v by two independent readers, October 2026; the syllables they read differently settled from the page by a third, who removed the show-through of f. 33r; see research/diffusa-est/staff-readings/README.md.</note>
          </bibl>
        </source>
      </sourceDesc>
    </fileDesc>
  </meiHead>
